# Copy this file to .env and put your own key in it.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. The keys are read by the SERVER only - never by the app.
# Gemini key, for tagging menus with features (extract_features).
GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# OpenRouter key, for the LLM question engine (https://openrouter.ai/keys).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...

# Optional server settings for the recommendation API (backend/recommend).
# The shared fixture only has 2026-09-29; without this the server uses today in Seoul.
# METCHU_MENU_DATE=2026-09-29
# Answers before the engine must guess. Default: no limit (unset or 0).
# METCHU_MAX_QUESTIONS=10
# Engine for a session whose client names none: decision_tree (default) or llm.
# The app picks one per session on its start screen; llm needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY above.
# METCHU_ENGINE=decision_tree
# Decision-tree policy: preference (default), greedy, or lookahead.
# METCHU_DT_POLICY=preference
# LLM engine only (backend/question_engines/llm): OpenRouter model ID and seconds per call.
# METCHU_LLM_MODEL=google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# Extra hostnames the server answers to, comma-separated (e.g. your LAN address).
# METCHU_ALLOWED_HOSTS=192.168.0.3
# `manage.py serve_public` opens a quick Cloudflare Tunnel with a random address.
# For a fixed address, set both of these to a named tunnel's token and hostname.
# The token is a secret, like the API key.
# METCHU_TUNNEL_TOKEN=...
# METCHU_PUBLIC_URL=https://metchu.example.com
# METCHU_LLM_TIMEOUT=10

# Shared database: the team's Supabase Postgres (backend/README.md, "Shared database").
# Copy the "Session pooler" URI from Supabase > Connect and put the DB password in it.
# Leave unset to use local SQLite (backend/db.sqlite3). Tests always use SQLite.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-<n>-ap-northeast-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
